\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The density repeats the ball assignment}
\date{2026-11-07}

\p{The coordinate formula multiplies #{x_k(r)} by
#{\bigl(\frac{\lambda}{p}\bigr)^{k/2}}. The cell density
multiplies #{x_k(r)} by #{(p\lambda)^{k/2}}. The second
factor equals the first multiplied by #{\lambda^k}.
Weighting #{F_k(r)} by the uniform probability #{p^{-k}}
returns #{M_k(r)}. The identity
for #{A} says that the value on a residue class modulo
#{p^{k-1}} is the arithmetic mean of the values on its #{p}
refinements. The law of the sequence #{(F_k)} is the image of
the projective law in \ref{fdip-00C3} under this fixed change
of scale.}
